<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carinthia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carinthia is an Alpine region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drava">Drava</a> valley and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klagenfurt">Klagenfurt</a> basin, with a small part now in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>. It grew from the early medieval Slavic principality of Carantania, became a duchy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> in 976 and passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in 1335. Today it is an Austrian federal state with its capital at Klagenfurt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carinthia.jpg" alt="Carinthia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Carinthia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under the Agilolfings Bavaria's forces fought Avars, Slavs and Lombards on its eastern and southern frontiers, and Duke Tassilo III subdued Carantania, roughly modern <b>Carinthia</b>, around 772.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-bavaria">Duchy of Bavaria · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The borders were settled in the peace treaties of Saint-Germain, Neuilly and Trianon and, with Italy, in the Treaty of Rapallo of 1920, while <b>Carinthia</b> voted to stay with Austria.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia">Kingdom of Yugoslavia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Following the death of Pope John XV, the German king Otto III chose his cousin Bruno of <b>Carinthia</b>, a member of the Salian dynasty, as pope.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/may-3">3 May in history</a></li><li><blockquote>After Samo's death around 658 they formed an independent principality centred on the Zollfeld plain near Karnburg in modern <b>Carinthia</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/carantania">Carantania</a></li><li><blockquote>The counts of Gorizia (Görz) appear around 1090 as advocates of the Patriarchate of Aquileia, with lands in Friuli, <b>Carinthia</b> and the Puster valley.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-gorizia">County of Gorizia</a></li><li><blockquote>A related branch became dukes of <b>Carinthia</b> from 1122.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-sponheim">County of Sponheim</a></li></ul></section>
